1. Consensual - Aapsi sehmati se/Means mutual, The agreement was consensual between both companies.
2. Impeccable - Bilkul perfect, The thing which has no mistake/ Nirdosh.
3. Scoundrel - Badmash aadmi, Beimaan ya dhokebaaz vyakti, Characterless person.
4. Grumpy - Chidchida, Gusse wala mood, Asani se irritate ho jana.
5. Consent - Permission dena. Eg: She gave her consent. 

6. Iron Fist: Kadi discipline se rule karna, Bahut sakhti se control karna. Zara si galati per bhi strict action lena.
 - Sentence: He rules with an iron fist.

7. Emergence (Noun): Start, beginning, rise. Ubharna.
 - The emergence of AI has caused worry among professionals across the globe.

8. Contamination: Kisi cheez ka ganda ya impure ho jana.
 - The food got contaminated due to poor hygiene.

9. Pathetic: Bahut bekaar, very bad, bilkul disappointing. Itna bura ki dekhkar taras aa jaye.
 - Don't act so pathetic. - Itna bekar/helpless mat behave karo.

10. Dabbler: Koi vyakti jo sirf thoda-thoda try karta hai, kisi kaam ko seriously ya deeply nahi seekhta.
 - He is just a dabbler in music.

11. Defuse: Shant Karna. To make a difficult or dangerous situation calmer by reducing or removing its cause.
 - United States President Donald Trump has once again claimed that he helped defuse a military conflict between India and Pakistan.

12. Histrionic: (adjective) Excessively theatrical or dramatic in character or style.
 - The widow's histronic screaming made the detectives suspicious.
(noun) melodramatic behaviour designed to attract attension.
 - By now, Anna was accustomed to her mother's histrionics.

13. Accustomed: if you are accustomed to something, you are used to it and it is not strange for you. किसी बात का आदी या अभ्यस्त ho jana. 
 - accustomed to: She quickly became accustomed to his messy ways.
 - I'm not accustomed to being treated like this.

14. Vague: not clearly expressed, known, described, or decided:
 - I do have a vague memory of meeting her many years ago.
not clear in shape, or not clearly seen:
 - Through the mist I could just make out a vague figure.
A vague person is not able to think clearly, or gives an impression of not thinking clearly in order to hide their real thoughts:
 - My aunt is incredibly vague - she can never remember where she puts things.

vaguely: I vaguely remembered having met her before.

15. Humblebrag: something you say which appears as if you are complaining or embarrassed, 
but is really a way of telling people about something that you are very proud of:
 - "I don't know why anybody would want my autograph!" he humblebragged.

16. assertion: a statement that you strongly believe is true:
 - I certainly don't agree with his assertion that men are better drivers than women

17. Observant: good or quick at noticing things:
 - "That's a new dress, isn't it?" "Yes, you are observant!"

18. Ineptitude: Lack of Skill or ability.
 - "Due to his financial ineptitude. Hank quickly lost all of his lottery winnings.

19. thrust (verb): to push suddenly and strongly: Mukhya Vishaya.
 - She thrust the money into his hand.
 - She thrust the papers at me (= towards me).
 - The main thrust of this seminar was the effect of AI in today's world.

20. foregone conclusion (noun): a result that is obvious before it happens:
 - The result of the election seems to be a foregone conclusion.

21. Turbulent (Adjective): Ashant - Involving a lot of sudden changes, arguments, or voilence.
 - Our neighboring country is facing a turbulent transition.
 - AI is emerging turbulently.

22. Erode: To slowly reduce or destroy something.
 - The court said that such content could erode public confidence in the judicial office.
 - Court ne kaha ki is tarah ke content se juidiciary vibhag mein logon ka bharosa khatam ho sakta hai.

23. Tout (Verb): Aggressively promote something.
 - The company touted the phone as the best on the market.
 - Company ne phone ko market ka best bol kar aggressively promote kiya.

24. Tout (Noun): Street seller/ticket bechne wala.
 - We were surrounded by ticket touts outside the stadium.
 - Stadium ke bahar ticket bechne wale log gher lete hain.

